<title>HONG KONG: Australia 1996 air cargo statistics detailed.</title>
<headline>Australia 1996 air cargo statistics detailed.</headline>
<byline>Jim Gilchrist</byline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong/Sydney was Australia's second busiest city to city air freight route last year, according to latest statistics issued by Australia's Department of Transport and Regional Development.</p>
<p>Auckland-Sydney remained the busiest city pair despite showing a 10 percent fall in air freight carried. Hong Kong-Sydney recorded a 14.8 percent increase. Osaka-Sydney showed the highest rise climbing 28.5 percent to 12,515 tonnes in the year ended June 1996.</p>
<p>The Department said the top ten city pairs listed below represent 49.4 percent of total freight tonnes traffic for the latest year compared with 50.3 percent in 94-95 and 49.4 percent in 93-94.</p>
<p> City Pair		 Year ended</p>
<p>			     June 94    June 95   June 96   Pct change</p>
<p>									Yr to June 96</p>
<p> Auckland/Sydney	 39,249     44,541    40,076    down 10.0pct</p>
<p> Hong Kong/Sydney	24,342     31,882    36,611    up   14.8</p>
<p> Singapore/Sydney	30,794     32,729    35,044    up    7.1</p>
<p> Los Angeles/ Sydney   29,765     33,686    30,553    down  9.3</p>
<p> Singapore/Melbourne   23,319     28,571    29,779    up    4.2</p>
<p> Auckland/Melbourne    22,293     22,742    28,275    up   24.3</p>
<p> Hong Kong/Melbourne   19,466     27,499    25,558    down  7.1</p>
<p> Tokyo/Sydney	    23,502     23.176    21,886    down  5.6</p>
<p> Singapore/Perth	 17,917     19,064    19,738    up    3.5</p>
<p> Osaka/Sydney	     4,466	9,742    12,515    up   28.5</p>
<p> Other city pairs     241,220    270,813   287,087    up    6.0</p>
<p> ALL CITY PAIRS	 476,335     544,448   567,122   up    4.2</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
